@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080

### 1. Register a new user (201 first time, 409 after that)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Arjun Mehta",
  "email": "Arjun@Example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### 2. Same email again, different capitals (expect 409 Conflict)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Arjun Again",
  "email": "arjun@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### 3. Bad input (expect 400 with a list of errors)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "",
  "email": "not-an-email",
  "password": "short"
}

### 4. Broken JSON (expect 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Arjun"

### 5. Log in (expect 200, an accessToken, and a Set-Cookie header)
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "arjun@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### 6. Wrong password (expect 401)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "arjun@example.com",
  "password": "wrongpassword"
}

### 7. Email that doesn't exist (expect the same 401 message as above)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "nobody@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### 8. Who am I, with the token from request 5 (expect 200 with Arjun's details)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### 9. Who am I, without a token (expect 401)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/me

### 10. Who am I, with a fake token (expect 401)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/me
Authorization: Bearer this.is.fake

### 11. Refresh (REST Client resends the cookie from request 5 automatically; expect 200 and a new Set-Cookie)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/refresh

### 12. Log out (expect 204 and a Set-Cookie that clears the cookie)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/logout

### 13. Refresh after logout (expect 401)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/refresh
